# Top-level ignores. The platform directories carry their own, narrower rules
# (android/.gitignore for Gradle + the gomobile .aar, ios/.gitignore for the
# xcframework, the xcodegen-generated project and Xcode build state), so this
# file deliberately covers only what those two don't: Go build output, the
# artifacts the examples and the WASM target write into the tree, and editor
# or OS cruft.

# Go build and test output. Binaries land next to their package when built
# without -o, so ignore the compiled test binaries and coverage profiles
# rather than trying to enumerate example binary names.
*.test
*.out
*.exe
coverage.html

# WASM target. index.html fetches main.wasm from this directory; it is a build
# product of `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build -o wasm/main.wasm ./wasm`.
# wasm_exec.js is NOT ignored — it is copied from the Go toolchain and tracked
# so the page works without a local Go install.
wasm/main.wasm

# htmlout demo output. Several examples render to a static page in the working
# directory (examples/chat -> social.html, examples/layout -> layout.html,
# examples/fintechapp -> materialwallet.html); these are regenerated by running
# the example, never committed.
social.html
layout.html
materialwallet.html

# Local scratch: agent/tool state that is per-checkout, not per-project.
.cats-todo/

# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
